{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15570-are-all-fallen-angels-created-equal","id":15570,"title":"Are all Fallen Angels created equal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-21T13:19:35-08:00","id":15570,"title":"Are all Fallen Angels created equal?","content":"Okay so I was wondering, the Unchained they can come from potentially any rank of angel right? The impression I'm getting so far is that they all start of relatively the same footing no matter what level of angel they were. Would this hold true even at the highest Ranks? Presumably the highest Angels of the God Machine are Rank 7 or 8. So would their fall be the same as any other Unchained? Perhaps the story of the Pain Prophet is actually about the very first Unchained?<br /> <br /> What ranks do think the Unchained are commonly of before they fall? Because their prefall stories seem to range drastically in scope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T13:57:15-08:00","id":15606,"title":"","content":"Rank before the Fall does not matter, as bring severed from ghe God-Machine leaves them with a very small amount of power; Primum 1, and a handful of Embeds. No matter what height an Angel falls from, they all hit rock bottom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T14:02:24-08:00","id":15612,"title":"","content":"What about the potential of an Angel falling into multiple Unchained?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T14:44:20-08:00","id":15635,"title":"","content":"I have no idea if that's canon but I'm stealing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T15:07:33-08:00","id":15653,"title":"","content":"I'd agree with atamajakki. For really powerful angels to even remain manifest, hundreds of humans have to be sacrificed. When they fall, they're disconnected from all of that fuel, their cover is burned into reality. After that's done, all that's left is the flickering flame of their free will (Primum 1). <br /> <br /> Another question I have is, what happens to fallen angels who weren't given a humanoid cover, like several of the ones in the GMC book? Perhaps, they're less likely to fall since even disguising as a human tends to give an angel more human-like thought patterns. Perhaps, the G-M gives all angels a humanoid cover &quot;just in case.&quot; I think the most likely answer is that angels who fall without a cover end up getting caught very quickly and reprocessed. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T15:23:30-08:00","id":15670,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that Primum, as described, isn't merely a power level. To quote the book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Primum, then, is a measure of how deeply integrated into reality a demon is, of how much identity she has as her own being rather than a fallen servant of the God Machine. </div> </div> </div>The power level of the angel in question doesn't really factor into it, especially since the process of Falling includes disconnecting one's self from the God Machine and its power.<br /> <br /> As for angels without cover, I think this has come up a couple of times in discussions and playtest scenarios. Long story short, it does happen that an angel can fall without a proper cover. Their survival, then, is going to likely depending on being able to make a pact quickly (maybe they were a cult leader before Falling and have access to someone they can go to) or other demons are going to have to find them and protect them for a bit and perhaps trade some favors for an unused soul pact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T15:56:59-08:00","id":15688,"title":"","content":"That all makes sense. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T16:01:32-08:00","id":15693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15570-are-all-fallen-angels-created-equal?p=15670#post15670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind that Primum, as described, isn't merely a power level. To quote the book:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The power level of the angel in question doesn't really factor into it, especially since the process of Falling includes disconnecting one's self from the God Machine and its power.<br /> <br /> As for angels without cover, I think this has come up a couple of times in discussions and playtest scenarios. Long story short, it does happen that an angel can fall without a proper cover. Their survival, then, is going to likely depending on being able to make a pact quickly (maybe they were a cult leader before Falling and have access to someone they can go to) or other demons are going to have to find them and protect them for a bit and perhaps trade some favors for an unused soul pact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Complexity though does factor in to the Fall, and beings of infinitely greater complexity are often of infinitely greater might, so I don't see why a truly up there angel can't fall in multiple levels and thus result in multiple Unchained. Much as in the same way in the old Demon the Fallen Truth and realization can take the form of a Song, a Mathmatic Formula, a Fight, a Geometric shape, ect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T05:34:29-08:00","id":16056,"title":"","content":"If other tier 4 entities are any example of how Archangels are, mechanically, i would assume each archangel is essentially a complex of multiple subprograms (subdivinities, if you will). Rather like True Fae or Archmages, the archangel would implement its programming through various subroutines, each requiring its own infrastructure. Thus, its far more likely that individual subdivinities would fall, and be cut off from the archangel. If the archangel fell, in its entirety.. it could go either way, i think, into multiple or into a singular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T03:02:40-08:00","id":16544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15570-are-all-fallen-angels-created-equal?p=16056#post16056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If other tier 4 entities are any example of how Archangels are, mechanically, i would assume each archangel is essentially a complex of multiple subprograms (subdivinities, if you will). Rather like True Fae or Archmages, the archangel would implement its programming through various subroutines, each requiring its own infrastructure. Thus, its far more likely that individual subdivinities would fall, and be cut off from the archangel. If the archangel fell, in its entirety.. it could go either way, i think, into multiple or into a singular.</div> </div> </div> </div>...or that this would be the end of the world as we know it. I mean, an archangel is really a huge chunk of the God Machine's power and influence, and the thought of something like THAT falling makes me think about the Testament of the Pain Prophet's furies..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T14:39:26-08:00","id":16805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15570-are-all-fallen-angels-created-equal?p=15653#post15653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd agree with atamajakki. For really powerful angels to even remain manifest, hundreds of humans have to be sacrificed. When they fall, they're disconnected from all of that fuel, their cover is burned into reality. After that's done, all that's left is the flickering flame of their free will (Primum 1).<br /> <br /> Another question I have is, what happens to fallen angels who weren't given a humanoid cover, like several of the ones in the GMC book? Perhaps, they're less likely to fall since even disguising as a human tends to give an angel more human-like thought patterns. Perhaps, the G-M gives all angels a humanoid cover &quot;just in case.&quot; I think the most likely answer is that angels who fall without a cover end up getting caught very quickly and reprocessed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is misleading though since every single Demon can Go Loud, and even for a new Demon going Loud is can be stronger then the weaker ranked angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T14:51:14-08:00","id":16811,"title":"","content":"I don't get you, missleading how?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T15:20:33-08:00","id":16822,"title":"","content":"I mean about how their only left with the flickering flame of Primum 1. When in truth that is only cause of their cover, anyone can go Loud and their Primum Roars to 10 when they do so.<br /> <br /> So this means if a weak angel falls, they actually would be stronger when going loud then they were as an Angel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T03:30:25-08:00","id":17059,"title":"","content":"For a brief time, after wich they'll be completly screwed, yes. Going out with a bang, as it were. As their actual Primum is 1, they will only have that one Cover. Burning it is not that a smart move as you seem to think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T05:18:09-08:00","id":17082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15570-are-all-fallen-angels-created-equal?p=17059#post17059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a brief time, after wich they'll be completly screwed, yes. Going out with a bang, as it were. As their actual Primum is 1, they will only have that one Cover. Burning it is not that a smart move as you seem to think.</div> </div> </div> </div>You presume much. Who said it was a smart move? All I said is they can do this. The downside of it has nothing to do with the power, the downside is an external concern that you will be swarmed by Angels. If push comes to shove any Demon can raise to such heights by burning their cover, meanwhile angels can't do this. So in a situation where say all they cared about was revenge or even saving one person they can toss everything to the wind to Go Loud, that can mean succeeding in what you set out to do.<br /> <br /> This makes me wonder if All Angels are made to be mighty but the low ranked ones actually have artificial restraints on their power so that the Godmachine will give them the most efficient power for the mission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T13:36:35-08:00","id":30558,"title":"","content":"I am totally using the Angel-Falls-and-Splits idea for an NPC ring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T14:53:14-08:00","id":30598,"title":"","content":"A story hook for an &quot;Angel Fall and Split&quot;-<br /> <br /> Once, there was an Archangel. Most of its life it worked just like a good part of the machine- until one day, it thought. That day, it fell, it essences is shattered into hundreds of Covers and personalities which didn't remembered that once they were one. You are one of those pieces, and lately demons are starting to get killed by angels without any warning- even those who were in deep cover. Somehow, the hunter angel just KNOWS where they are. Eventually, you find the horrifying truth- that before your fall you were a part of an Archangel- and than discover something even more horrible. Not all of the Archangel has fell. A single part of it has kept its trust in the Machine, and after years of proving it was loyal the God Machine has decided to give it a chance to retain its former glory. The only catch- it must find and kill all of its former parts of self, becoming one with them, and once it would collect the essence of all of his &quot;shards&quot; it would rise again as an Archangel of the God machine- and with each shard it gathers, the closer it returns to gain its former glory. And because you once were part of it, it can feel you even while you are under Cover, just like you can know where your toes are. There no where to run, no way to hide. it is coming, and it wants his shards back- and, unfortunately, you are one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}